# Nothing built ever goes in. The installer is produced from openphantom_installer.iss with
# Inno Setup and the extractor from src/is3_extract with CMake; see README.md.
#
# The wildcard covers a second configure alongside the first, build-audit or build-x86 or
# whatever it gets called. Those are as untrackable as build/ itself and easy to commit by
# accident, because git shows them and the reviewer sees one more directory rather than
# thirty megabytes.
build*/
*.obj
*.pdb
*.exp
*.lib
*.ilk
*.exe

# ...but dist/ is shipped content, not build output. Everything the installer carries lives
# there and is tracked on purpose, third-party binaries included, which the rule above would
# otherwise swallow without saying so.
!dist/**

# Inno Setup writes these beside a script while it works.
*.iss.bak
*.tmp

# A release archive dropped in the checkout to test a pinned build against. The one that counts is on
# the releases page and the script downloads it.
*.zip
